        "parms": "# mtof ftom dbtoa atodb — pitch and level\nmtof turns a MIDI note number into a frequency in Hz, with note 69 at 440 Hz, and ftom turns a frequency back. dbtoa turns decibels into a linear amplitude, and atodb turns it back. Fractions pass through: note 69.5 is a quarter tone above A.\nMax's dbtoa and atodb count decibels from full scale, an amplitude of 1 being 0 dB. Here 1 is 100 dB: subtract 100 for decibels from full scale. Every result is finite: 0 Hz gives note -1500, an amplitude of 0 gives 0 dB.",
